  "query_preview": "(Today through Tuesday)...\nIssued at 247 AM EDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nSurface analysis early this morning shows strong high pressure over \nNew England, maintaining control of the weather across points east \nof the Mississippi. A weak upper trough was found over WI and IL, \npushing east. Ahead of this trough an area of clouds were seen \nacross Indiana, while water vapor showed subsidence in the wake of \nthe trough over IA/IL and the southern plains. Winds were light to \ncalm across central Indiana dew points were in the upper 40s or \nlower 50s.\n\nToday and Tonight...\n\nMore above normal temperatures and more sunshine is expected across \nCentral Indiana today. Weak ridging aloft is expected to push across \nCentral Indiana today as the clouds and upper trough over the area \ndepart early this morning. This will lead to a mostly sunny day and \ncontinued warm temperatures. The surface high pressure system to the \neast will continue to provide a warm an southerly flow of air to \nCentral Indiana, allowing highs to reach the middle 70s and a few \nupper 70s. Time heights and forecast soundings show a dry column \ntoday and tonight with subsidence in play.\n\nThursday and Friday.... \n\nWest to southwest flow is expected to be in place on Thursday, \ntransitioning to a upper ridge on Friday. Little to no forcing \ndynamics are in expected to pass on Thursday. The upper ridge looks \nto protect Indiana from any forcing on Friday. Meanwhile at the \nsurface, a cold front will drop out of the upper midwest on Thursday \nafternoon and stall over Central Indiana. This really is a the tail \nof the front extending well into Quebec and there is little forcing \nor moisture associated with it, as it is more of a cusp between two \nhigh pressure systems. Forecast soundings through this period show a \nfew clouds on Thursday night, but never come close to saturation. \nThus more dry and warm weather will be expected. Southwest flow \nahead of the front on Thursday will allow for highs to reach the \nupper 70s to around 80 on Thursday, with cooler values expected in \nthe wake of the front for Friday.\n\nSaturday through Tuesday...\n\nThe upper pattern during this time suggests upper ridging over the \nplains on Saturday, pushing through Indiana on Sunday and Monday \nbefore reaching the east coast by Tuesday. As the flow become more \nsouthwesterly on the windward side of the ridge on Sunday through \nTuesday, models suggest waves of upper forcing embedded within the \nflow pushing toward Indiana. Furthermore, Isentropic surfaces show \nan ongoing pattern of broad lift. Within the lower levels, high \npressure is suggested to over the eastern Great Lakes and Middle \nAtlantic states on Saturday and Sunday before pushed off the coast \nfor Monday and Tuesday. The lower level east or southeasterly flow \nwill allow for an overrunning setup on Saturday through Monday. By \nTuesday, a deeper low pressure system over the southern plains is \nsuggested to set up allowing an associated warm front to reside over \nCentral IL and Indiana. Best chances for rain at this time look to \nbe Sunday, Sunday Night and Tuesday, but with all these ingredients \nin place through this period, smaller chances cannot be ruled out \nyet on late Saturday and Monday. Due to the cloud cover and \nprecipitation during the period, expect lows in the 50s, but highs \nmainly reaching only the mid to upper 60s. Normal high temperatures \nfor this time of year is in the upper 50s.",
